  <!-- SECTION 4: SETUP -->
  <div class="sec-mark" id="setup">7-STEP SETUP</div>
  <div class="prose"><h2 id="complete-setup-the-makecom-webhook-method">Complete Setup: The Make.com Webhook Method</h2><p>This method fires from Shopify&rsquo;s backend on payment confirmation: no browser dependency, no thank-you page required, no Shopify app to install. Before step 4, check Shopify&rsquo;s Facebook &amp; Instagram app: if its data sharing is set to Enhanced or Maximum, Shopify already sends Meta&rsquo;s Conversions API, so skip step 4 rather than send Meta every purchase twice.</p></div>
  <p style="border-left:3px solid #2dd4bf;padding:6px 14px;margin:16px 0;font-size:13px;font-family:monospace;"><strong>GOOGLE ADS:</strong> <a href="/shopify-google-ads-conversion-tracking/">For Google Ads, the free fix is enhanced conversions in Shopify&rsquo;s Google &amp; YouTube app; why a Make.com upload is a weaker route.</a></p>
  <div class="step-cards">
    <div class="step-card">
      <div class="step-num-col"><div class="step-n">1</div></div>
      <div class="step-body">
        <div class="step-title">Create your free Make.com account</div>
        <div class="step-desc">Sign up at Make.com: no credit card required. The free plan gives you 1,000 credits/month. Most modules use one credit each time they run, so this scenario uses about one credit per module per order; the scenario history shows the real figure. Create a new scenario and name it &ldquo;Shopify Server-Side Tracking&rdquo;.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card">
      <div class="step-num-col"><div class="step-n">2</div></div>
      <div class="step-body">
        <div class="step-title">Add a Webhooks trigger module</div>
        <div class="step-desc">In your new scenario, click the empty module circle. Search for <strong>Webhooks</strong> &rarr; <strong>Custom webhook</strong>. Click Add, name it &ldquo;Shopify order webhook&rdquo;, save. Make.com generates a unique webhook URL: <strong>copy it now</strong>. This URL is your secure endpoint that Shopify will POST order data to.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card">
      <div class="step-num-col"><div class="step-n">3</div></div>
      <div class="step-body">
        <div class="step-title">Add the Shopify Order Payment webhook</div>
        <div class="step-desc">In Shopify Admin &rarr; <strong>Settings &rarr; Notifications &rarr; Webhooks</strong>, click Create webhook. Set:<br>
          <span class="step-path">Event: <strong>Order payment</strong> &bull; Format: JSON &bull; URL: paste your Make.com webhook URL</span>
          Save. Shopify will POST the full order payload to Make.com every time a payment is confirmed, not on order creation, not on fulfilment, on confirmed payment only.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card meta">
      <div class="step-num-col"><div class="step-n">4</div></div>
      <div class="step-body">
        <div class="step-title"><span class="step-platform-tag spt-meta">META</span> Add Meta CAPI HTTP module</div>
        <div class="step-desc">Add an <strong>HTTP &rarr; Make a request</strong> module. Configure:<br>
          <span class="step-path">URL: https://graph.facebook.com/v24.0/YOUR_PIXEL_ID/events?access_token=YOUR_TOKEN<br>Method: POST &bull; Body type: Raw &bull; Content type: JSON</span>
          <em style="display:block;margin-top:6px;font-size:12px;color:#93a09a;">Use the current Graph API version: Meta deprecates older versions roughly every two years. Check the <a href="https://developers.facebook.com/docs/graph-api/changelog/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:#93a09a;text-decoration:underline;">Graph API changelog</a> for the latest <code>vXX.0</code> and swap it into the URL.</em>
          In the body, map: <span class="code-ref">event_name</span> = Purchase, <span class="code-ref">event_id</span> = order ID, <span class="code-ref">event_time</span> = <span class="code-ref">formatDate(1.created_at; "X")</span>, <span class="code-ref">action_source</span> = website, <span class="code-ref">value</span> = order total, <span class="code-ref">currency</span> = currency code. In user_data: <span class="code-ref">sha256(lower(trim(email)))</span> and the hashed phone, plus the order&rsquo;s IP and user agent unhashed. Set the module to return an error on a failed request, and add a Break error handler.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card google">
      <div class="step-num-col"><div class="step-n">5</div></div>
      <div class="step-body">
        <div class="step-title"><span class="step-platform-tag spt-google">GOOGLE</span> Turn on enhanced conversions in the Google &amp; YouTube app</div>
        <div class="step-desc">Google Ads is not a Make.com step. Shopify&rsquo;s order data has no Google click ID for a server upload to use, and Google is moving its click conversion upload to the Data Manager API. Instead, in Shopify&rsquo;s <strong>Google &amp; YouTube app</strong>, open <strong>Settings &rarr; Google Ads settings</strong>, find <strong>Enhanced conversions</strong>, select <strong>Turn on</strong> and accept Google&rsquo;s customer data terms. <a href="/shopify-google-ads-conversion-tracking/">The full Google Ads guide</a> covers the limits.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card tiktok">
      <div class="step-num-col"><div class="step-n">6</div></div>
      <div class="step-body">
        <div class="step-title"><span class="step-platform-tag spt-tiktok">TIKTOK</span> Add TikTok Events API module</div>
        <div class="step-desc">Add a third HTTP module. POST to <span class="code-ref">https://business-api.tiktok.com/open_api/v1.3/event/track/</span>.<br>
          <strong>Critical:</strong> use <span class="code-ref">event_name</span> = <strong>CompletePayment</strong>, not &ldquo;Purchase&rdquo;. TikTok&rsquo;s algorithm only recognises CompletePayment as a purchase event. Put hashed email and phone, and the order&rsquo;s IP address and user agent, under <span class="code-ref">data[].user</span>, with <span class="code-ref">event_source</span> = web and your pixel ID as <span class="code-ref">event_source_id</span>. The <a href="/tiktok-events-api-shopify/">TikTok guide</a> has the full body.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="step-card">
      <div class="step-num-col"><div class="step-n">7</div></div>
